      heading: "Working with a developer 1.5 hours away rather than across town",
      paragraphs: [
        `India is 1.5 hours ahead of the UAE, so a Dubai working day sits almost entirely inside ours. In practical terms that is closer in working hours than a European supplier and far closer than an American one.`,
        `The rhythm on a Dubai project: a weekly video call scheduled Monday to Thursday Dubai time, a shared task board you can read whenever you like, a staging link that always shows the current state, and WhatsApp for the short questions that would otherwise become email. A question sent at the end of your working day is usually answered the same evening. Launches are scheduled midweek in Dubai morning hours, never on a Thursday evening and never on a Friday.`,
        `We work to your week, not ours. The UAE's Saturday–Sunday weekend, the shortened Friday much of the private sector keeps, and the UAE public holiday calendar are what we plan around, which also means we build those assumptions into the site itself rather than leaving a European default in the booking form. The detail on that is in the locale section of <a href='/uae/website-development-dubai/'>website development in Dubai</a>.`,
        `What remote does not solve: anything physical. No meetings in your office, no photography, no site survey, no collecting a document, no sitting beside your client in a pitch. If one of those is a requirement rather than a preference, hire in Dubai. We would rather lose the work on the first call than three weeks in.`,
      ],
